From: red-Geck0 <127088086+red-Geck0@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 12:42:11 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 69/72] feat(hybrid): Windows GPU statistics in the performance
 overlay

The overlay's GPU rows were filled only on macOS (IOAccelerator): on
Windows the compact panel showed "GPU n/a" and the full panel only the
Vulkan device name and budget. hostGpuWindows.cpp now samples the
adapter the renderer created its device on (SetHostGpuAdapter, by the
Vulkan device LUID):

- PDH "GPU Engine" / "GPU Adapter Memory" / "GPU Process Memory" (the
  counters Task Manager shows, every vendor, English names so any
  Windows language works): utilization of the busiest engine, 3D,
  compute, copy and video engines, the emulator's own share, dedicated
  and shared memory of the device and of the emulator;
- DXGI: adapter name, dedicated/shared memory sizes, driver version;
- Intel Graphics Control Library (ControlLib.dll from the Intel
  driver, no Level Zero): clock, power from the energy counter,
  temperature where the GPU has a sensor, throttle reasons, Xe cores;
- D3DKMT adapter/node performance data: temperature, fan, power share
  and clock on drivers that report them (NVIDIA, AMD);
- ACPI thermal zones as the SoC temperature of an integrated GPU
  without a sensor of its own.

Everything is loaded at run time and optional. Tested in game on an
Intel Arc B390 (Xe3, integrated, driver 32.0.101.9175): the compact
panel reads "GPU 93% 2300 MHz 17.0 W 74 C SoC" in the world map, the
full panel the 3D engine, the emulator's share and shared memory.
D3DKMT perf data and the IGCL temperature are zero/unsupported there,
so the panel shows the SoC temperature (ACPI).

